    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28972" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mētrŏpŏlis</span></b> , is,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητρόπολις</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city from which
				other cities have been colonized, a mother-city;</i> also, the
				<i>chief city, metropolis</i> of a province
			(post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 11,
				21</span></i>; Cod. Th. 13, 3, 11.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metropolis et arx mentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. adv. Jovin. 2, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
